{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB12332 - MONDO_18172",
  "verbalization": "Rucaparib, a poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase inhibitor, is implicated in the treatment of ovarian tumors through its ability to target cancer cell proliferation. The evidence suggests that Rucaparib may be repurposed for the treatment of Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor Of Ovary, as it is linked to Cisplatin, which is a known chemotherapy agent used in the management of ovarian tumors. The shared indication with Cisplatin implies a potential mechanism of action that could be relevant to the pathogenesis of these tumors. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Rucaparib to Cisplatin, and subsequently to Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor Of Ovary, suggests a possible role in the treatment of these cancers through a common therapeutic target. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Rucaparib to be used in the management of ovarian tumors, particularly those associated with familial ovarian cancer, by leveraging its known efficacy against Cisplatin.",
